58 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 42 0 R
/T (Worker Assistance Platform designed to bring these workflows into one mobile application. Its proposed feature set includes digital patient registration and records, local/offline data handling, cloud synchronization through Firebase, priority-based follow-up, reminders, reports, patient field mapping, an AI-assisted health- information chatbot, and English/Kannada language and voice interaction. The system is organized into presentation, business- logic, data/service, and device/network layers. The project is reported as approximately 80% complete at the Review-3stage. The current work includes the main application interface and several core modules; full integration and end-to-end testing of synchronization, mapping, and voice-related features remain in progress. This paper describes the problem, architecture, workflows, implementation status, planned evaluation, and limitations. CareConnect is intended to assist with information organization and follow-up, not to replace qualified medical judgment.)
/E (Worker Assistance Platform designed to bring these workflows into one mobile application. Its proposed feature set includes digital patient registration and records, local/offline data handling, cloud synchronization through Firebase, priority-based follow-up, reminders, reports, patient field mapping, an AI-assisted health- information chatbot, and English/Kannada language and voice interaction. The system is organized into presentation, business- logic, data/service, and device/network layers. The project is reported as approximately 80% complete at the Review-3stage. The current work includes the main application interface and several core modules; full integration and end-to-end testing of synchronization, mapping, and voice-related features remain in progress. This paper describes the problem, architecture, workflows, implementation status, planned evaluation, and limitations. CareConnect is intended to assist with information organization and follow-up, not to replace qualified medical judgment.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [11]
>>
