/T (Offline-first design allows selected operations to continue on a device when the network is unavailable. Local storage can keep records accessible during field work, while a later synchronization process can transfer changes to a cloud service. CareConnect identifies Room as the local database and Firebase Firestore as the cloud data service. The project still requires complete integration testing to establish how synchronization behaves under interrupted connectivity and conflicting updates.)
