592 0 obj
<<
/Title (Worker Assistance Platform designed to bring these workflows into one mobile application. Its proposed feature set includes digital patient registration and records, local/offline data handling, cloud synchronization through Firebase, priority-based follow-up, reminders, reports, patient field mapping, an AI-assisted health- information chatbot, and English/Kannada language and voice interaction. The system is organized into presentation, business- logic, data/service, and device/network layers. The project is reported as approximately 80% complete at the Review-3stage. The current work includes the main application interface and several core modules; full integration and end-to-end testing of synchronization, mapping, and voice-related features remain in progress. This paper describes the problem, architecture, workflows, implementation status, planned evaluation, and limitations. CareConnect is intended to assist with information organization and follow-up, not to replace qualified medical judgment.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 568 0 R
/Prev 579 0 R
/Next 580 0 R
>>
endobj
593 0 obj
<<
/Title (When information is stored in notebooks, paper files, or separate applications, workers may need to search across multiple sources to understand a patient's recent activity or next follow-up date. This creates additional work and can make it harder to maintain a consistent view of pending tasks. Network access is another practical concern: a mobile application that depends on a continuous internet connection may become difficult to use during field visits. CareConnect addresses these needs through a unified Android application. The project combines patient management with an offline-first approach, follow-up prioritization, reminders, mapping, reports, and general health-information access. Its design also considers English and Kannada language support and voice interaction, with the aim of making the application more accessible)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 569 0 R
/Prev 581 0 R
/Next 594 0 R
>>
endobj
